1
00:02:30,807 --> 00:02:32,200
I'm faster than you!

2
00:02:32,240 --> 00:02:33,459
I'm not gonna lose!

3
00:02:33,500 --> 00:02:34,560
What gives?

4
00:02:34,600 --> 00:02:36,460
See ya later!

5
00:02:41,806 --> 00:02:43,246
Out of the way, out of the way!

6
00:02:53,855 --> 00:02:57,440
Grandfather, that looks like fun! Want to try it?!

7
00:02:57,565 --> 00:02:58,576
Well, let's do it...

8
00:02:58,914 --> 00:02:59,861
But is it safe?

9
00:03:00,024 --> 00:03:01,024
Who knows!

10
00:03:01,550 --> 00:03:02,820
Here we go!

11
00:03:06,320 --> 00:03:08,973
Don't let him get past you, Mister!

12
00:03:15,093 --> 00:03:16,239
How's that?!

13
00:03:17,101 --> 00:03:19,133
Woohoo! I won!

14
00:03:19,460 --> 00:03:21,846
Pull the brake! Come on, hurry!

15
00:03:22,040 --> 00:03:24,000
Pull the brake!

16
00:03:24,730 --> 00:03:26,606
How do you stop this thing?!

17
00:03:27,219 --> 00:03:28,400
Help me!

18
00:03:31,110 --> 00:03:32,110
Opal! Go!

19
00:03:33,700 --> 00:03:34,980
Help!

20
00:03:39,780 --> 00:03:40,900
Mister!

21
00:03:42,120 --> 00:03:43,353
How terrible!

22
00:03:43,750 --> 00:03:44,750
I won't let them get away!

23
00:03:44,874 --> 00:03:46,713
Stop that carriage!

24
00:03:47,907 --> 00:03:49,673
Grandpa!

25
00:03:49,980 --> 00:03:51,100
Grandpa, hold on!

26
00:03:51,279 --> 00:03:54,119
Hey, look right here! Grandpa!

27
00:03:54,889 --> 00:03:56,646
Huh? What's this?

28
00:03:57,240 --> 00:04:01,200
Oh, right. This is from that hit-and-run carriage.

29
00:04:08,270 --> 00:04:10,746
Wait! Stop!

30
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:15,626
I won't let you get away with a hit-and-run!

31
00:04:23,235 --> 00:04:24,835
That was a close one...

32
00:04:39,433 --> 00:04:42,940
Old man, if we hadn't treated you in time, you would've died.

33
00:04:44,170 --> 00:04:47,353
Mister, the hit-and-run driver got away. I'm sorry.

34
00:04:47,535 --> 00:04:49,780
Don't worry, I'll definitely catch 'em!

35
00:04:50,040 --> 00:04:53,454
Grandfather, if we use this metal piece dropped by the carriage as a clue,

36
00:04:53,479 --> 00:04:55,680
we can definitely catch them. Really!

37
00:04:56,875 --> 00:05:00,580
Let's go, Sapphire. I'm gonna punch that guy! Definitely!

38
00:05:23,440 --> 00:05:25,580
- Get out of here, you brat!
- No, no, no.

39
00:05:26,753 --> 00:05:27,939
It's Tink!

40
00:05:28,460 --> 00:05:31,104
Did you think you could buy medicine with a measly ten yen, 

41
00:05:31,129 --> 00:05:32,666
you complete and total idiot?!

42
00:05:32,896 --> 00:05:36,059
Ten yen is all I have, you stupid, stupid, stingy idiot!

43
00:05:37,290 --> 00:05:40,940
Father in heaven, I'm sorry for talking bad about others.

44
00:05:41,290 --> 00:05:42,126
Tink!

45
00:05:42,600 --> 00:05:45,401
Opal! Sapphire! Thank goodness!

46
00:05:45,426 --> 00:05:47,793
Tink, why did you come to buy medicine?

47
00:05:48,360 --> 00:05:51,705
Well, a rabbit and a raccoon dog got hit by a carriage.

48
00:05:51,729 --> 00:05:53,753
It was a scary black carriage.

49
00:05:55,689 --> 00:05:57,319
What? A black carriage?

50
00:06:08,280 --> 00:06:09,486
Those poor things...

51
00:06:10,360 --> 00:06:13,240
Hey, do you know anything about the black carriage that hit you?

52
00:06:17,910 --> 00:06:19,100
Yeah, got it.

53
00:06:19,880 --> 00:06:22,984
They don't know whose carriage it is,

54
00:06:23,009 --> 00:06:25,820
but it passes through the Northern Forest every day around this time.

55
00:06:27,730 --> 00:06:29,520
The Northern Forest? <i>Alright!</i>

56
00:06:37,340 --> 00:06:38,860
It definitely passes through here.

57
00:06:39,658 --> 00:06:42,440
Huh? These fallen leaves haven't been stepped on yet.

58
00:06:43,496 --> 00:06:45,806
Which means it hasn't passed by yet today.

59
00:06:50,320 --> 00:06:51,600
It's coming from over there!

60
00:06:52,610 --> 00:06:53,640
Alright, bring it on!

61
00:07:09,356 --> 00:07:10,376
Sapphire!

62
00:07:15,456 --> 00:07:16,292
Wait, 

63
00:07:16,436 --> 00:07:18,340
this is the forest behind the castle.

64
00:07:23,680 --> 00:07:25,191
That's strange. Even people from the castle

65
00:07:25,216 --> 00:07:26,699
aren't supposed to use this back gate.

66
00:07:29,916 --> 00:07:31,889
I wonder who this cloaked man is.

67
00:07:39,540 --> 00:07:41,705
Open up! Open up! I said open up!

68
00:07:41,729 --> 00:07:42,920
What, you brat?!

69
00:07:43,170 --> 00:07:45,060
Open this door!

70
00:07:45,085 --> 00:07:46,599
No one is allowed through here!

71
00:07:46,623 --> 00:07:49,155
But someone dressed in black just went in!

72
00:07:49,180 --> 00:07:50,540
Nobody went in!

73
00:07:50,975 --> 00:07:53,873
Shut up! I clearly saw someone go in!

74
00:07:53,898 --> 00:07:55,495
Open up! I said open up!

75
00:07:55,520 --> 00:07:57,099
Shut up! Go away!

76
00:07:57,735 --> 00:08:00,280
Damn it! Open up! Open the door, you idiot!

77
00:08:01,320 --> 00:08:03,395
You refuse to open it? Fine...

78
00:08:04,059 --> 00:08:07,260
I won't move from here until you do! I won't budge!

79
00:08:28,210 --> 00:08:30,348
So that man really was the hit-and-run culprit.

80
00:08:31,179 --> 00:08:31,901
It fits.

81
00:08:32,499 --> 00:08:33,846
This is definitely the place.

82
00:08:36,415 --> 00:08:38,380
<i>I had no idea there were stairs like this here.</i>

83
00:08:42,253 --> 00:08:44,720
<i>I didn't know there was a secret corridor here.</i>

84
00:08:55,089 --> 00:08:57,248
I hope no one saw you.

85
00:08:57,272 --> 00:08:58,833
Don't worry about that.

86
00:08:59,455 --> 00:09:00,559
<i>Duralumin's henchmen...</i>

87
00:09:03,780 --> 00:09:04,640
<i>Someone's coming!</i>

88
00:09:09,440 --> 00:09:10,440
<i>Who could it be?</i>

89
00:09:15,809 --> 00:09:16,740
<i>Father!</i>

90
00:09:16,789 --> 00:09:19,260
I'm here with warm wishes for His Majesty!

91
00:09:22,339 --> 00:09:25,693
<i>I wonder what Father is secretly discussing with those guys.</i>

92
00:09:27,460 --> 00:09:27,961
<i>Still,</i>

93
00:09:28,165 --> 00:09:30,635
<i>he's with Duralumin and that hit-and-run driver,</i>

94
00:09:30,959 --> 00:09:32,466
<i>so I hope it's nothing bad.</i>

95
00:09:36,753 --> 00:09:40,741
Very well, Your Majesty. I'll deliver it as soon as it's ready.

96
00:09:41,132 --> 00:09:42,980
Ah, yes. Thank you.

97
00:09:47,928 --> 00:09:49,178
Well then, I shall take my leave...

98
00:09:49,202 --> 00:09:50,220
Now then...

99
00:09:58,969 --> 00:09:59,491
Hold it!

100
00:10:00,428 --> 00:10:02,780
What were you discussing with the King and Duralumin?

101
00:10:05,309 --> 00:10:07,171
You're another spy, aren't you?

102
00:10:07,195 --> 00:10:10,220
You came to pry into the new weapon I invented!

103
00:10:12,484 --> 00:10:15,873
I'm no spy! I'm a friend of the old man you hit and ran!

104
00:10:17,569 --> 00:10:20,119
So it was you from back then! Persistent bastard!

105
00:10:21,020 --> 00:10:24,119
You hit-and-run coward! I'll teach you a lesson for that old man!

106
00:10:25,579 --> 00:10:28,286
Acting all fancy, you little brat!

107
00:10:28,820 --> 00:10:29,820
Let's go!

108
00:10:36,150 --> 00:10:37,920
Looks like you're cornered!

109
00:10:43,080 --> 00:10:44,200
Over here! Over here!

110
00:10:57,786 --> 00:10:58,773
Are you running away?!

111
00:10:59,069 --> 00:10:59,964
Don't panic!

112
00:11:00,782 --> 00:11:03,146
I'll give you a taste of my new weapon!

113
00:11:03,760 --> 00:11:04,653
What?!

114
00:11:05,480 --> 00:11:06,480
Whoops!

115
00:11:11,750 --> 00:11:12,880
Is that all you've got?

116
00:11:16,849 --> 00:11:19,020
I've got plenty of better weapons!

117
00:11:19,125 --> 00:11:20,606
Now it's my turn!

118
00:11:28,009 --> 00:11:31,920
Another one of my inventions—the Birdlime Beast!

119
00:11:31,965 --> 00:11:34,326
Coward! Stop using such weird tricks!

120
00:11:35,935 --> 00:11:39,340
Struggle all you want. I'm a busy man. So long!

121
00:11:39,671 --> 00:11:42,186
Wait! Are you running away? You coward!

122
00:11:43,149 --> 00:11:45,320
Birdlime, huh? This should come off easily!

123
00:11:47,781 --> 00:11:51,020
That's it! There's grape juice in this barrel! It might dissolve the birdlime!

124
00:11:52,800 --> 00:11:54,773
Whoa! Just as I thought!

125
00:11:55,140 --> 00:11:56,140
Wait!

126
00:11:58,235 --> 00:12:00,915
Hey! Lord Sapphire! This area is off-limits!

127
00:12:00,940 --> 00:12:01,940
This is no time for that!

128
00:12:02,959 --> 00:12:04,659
Shorty! Which way did the black carriage go?

129
00:12:05,689 --> 00:12:07,626
Come on, don't panic.

130
00:12:10,186 --> 00:12:11,240
What a smell!

131
00:12:12,669 --> 00:12:14,286
This stuff really stinks.

132
00:12:17,569 --> 00:12:21,110
I splashed it onto that black carriage, so if we follow the scent,

133
00:12:21,135 --> 00:12:23,240
we'll track them down for sure.

134
00:12:24,160 --> 00:12:25,240
Sorry, sorry.

135
00:12:37,849 --> 00:12:39,840
We've come pretty deep into the mountains.

136
00:12:40,265 --> 00:12:42,640
Taking so long... I'm getting hungry.

137
00:12:44,249 --> 00:12:45,249
It must be inside here.

138
00:12:46,490 --> 00:12:48,180
How do you open this thing?

139
00:12:51,609 --> 00:12:52,800
It won't budge at all.

140
00:12:55,420 --> 00:12:59,326
Guess we'll have to look for a way in from the top of the mountain, Shorty.

141
00:13:12,879 --> 00:13:15,260
Open the ceiling hatch for the test flight!

142
00:13:16,438 --> 00:13:17,499
Open the upper hatch!

143
00:13:29,099 --> 00:13:30,929
There's no way in anywhere.

144
00:13:51,770 --> 00:13:55,160
I finally made a deal with the King and Grand Duke Duralumin!

145
00:13:55,460 --> 00:13:57,540
They're going to buy this flying battleship!

146
00:14:09,976 --> 00:14:12,920
Still, if I do say so myself, this flying battleship turned out splendidly.

147
00:14:14,239 --> 00:14:18,986
I see... so what Father was talking to Duralumin about was buying this!

148
00:14:20,813 --> 00:14:23,213
Still, what a terrifying new weapon.

149
00:14:37,409 --> 00:14:40,913
Let's punish that hit-and-run jerk, Sapphire!

150
00:14:41,667 --> 00:14:42,085
Yeah,

151
00:14:42,383 --> 00:14:44,880
that's right! We're gonna smash that terrifying new weapon to pieces!

152
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:45,606
Agreed!

153
00:14:45,720 --> 00:14:46,240
All right!

154
00:14:46,545 --> 00:14:47,698
Preparation complete!

155
00:14:55,480 --> 00:14:56,480
What's wrong?

156
00:15:00,140 --> 00:15:00,840
Don't run!

157
00:15:00,841 --> 00:15:02,240
It's those brats!

158
00:15:02,820 --> 00:15:03,820
Get 'em!

159
00:15:12,200 --> 00:15:13,020
I've got a great idea!

160
00:15:13,175 --> 00:15:15,526
Hey, release the steam to blind the enemy!

161
00:15:15,570 --> 00:15:16,570
All right!

162
00:15:18,903 --> 00:15:19,579
Let's see...

163
00:15:19,603 --> 00:15:21,600
This must be it.

164
00:15:40,620 --> 00:15:41,986
Take this!

165
00:15:43,259 --> 00:15:47,085
Try it if you dare! This brat's life is mine.

166
00:15:47,109 --> 00:15:48,105
Sapphire!

167
00:15:48,260 --> 00:15:48,993
Shorty!

168
00:15:49,300 --> 00:15:52,340
Sapphire, forget about me! Just get him!

169
00:15:52,380 --> 00:15:52,979
Wait...

170
00:15:53,065 --> 00:15:54,480
That's it, good girl.

171
00:15:56,049 --> 00:15:57,893
Now, hurry up and let Shorty go!

172
00:15:59,209 --> 00:16:00,380
Get down!

173
00:16:10,479 --> 00:16:12,240
Get rid of that brat!

174
00:16:14,260 --> 00:16:14,886
Move!

175
00:16:16,906 --> 00:16:18,120
Hurry, cut the ropes!

176
00:16:49,309 --> 00:16:54,060
Starboard clear, course set, engines running smooth... Steady as she goes!

177
00:16:54,164 --> 00:16:56,433
"Steady as she goes" my ass, you idiot!

178
00:16:57,429 --> 00:17:00,320
So, how do you like riding a flying battleship?

179
00:17:00,750 --> 00:17:02,973
Why is this thing such a monster?

180
00:17:04,419 --> 00:17:06,892
Scream while you can. Once we get higher,

181
00:17:06,916 --> 00:17:10,140
I'll drop you and squash you flat!

182
00:17:10,754 --> 00:17:12,299
Squash me flat?

183
00:17:13,469 --> 00:17:14,476
Sapphire!

184
00:17:15,980 --> 00:17:18,940
Go ahead and cry while you still can.

185
00:17:29,996 --> 00:17:32,720
Right then, looks like we've hit just the right altitude.

186
00:17:34,920 --> 00:17:38,759
That's high! Dropping from this high up, you've got to be kidding me!

187
00:17:39,306 --> 00:17:41,453
Alright, this is where you get off.

188
00:17:41,784 --> 00:17:44,340
Help! Sapphire!

189
00:17:45,999 --> 00:17:46,639
What?!

190
00:17:49,520 --> 00:17:49,960
Hey!

191
00:17:50,220 --> 00:17:51,520
I've finally caught up to you!

192
00:17:51,680 --> 00:17:52,680
Just what I was waiting for!

193
00:17:53,064 --> 00:17:54,266
What a persistent pest!

194
00:17:54,544 --> 00:17:55,544
Shorty, are you okay?

195
00:17:56,540 --> 00:17:58,040
I knew you'd come!

196
00:17:59,079 --> 00:18:02,080
Prepare yourself this time!

197
00:18:33,306 --> 00:18:35,706
Save me!

198
00:18:54,019 --> 00:18:55,019
Hey, what's that?

199
00:18:55,519 --> 00:18:58,680
What? It's no bird! No, wait... that's a flying ship!

200
00:18:58,879 --> 00:19:00,773
Come now, Your Majesty!

201
00:19:00,840 --> 00:19:04,026
The flying battleship you ordered is complete!

202
00:19:04,939 --> 00:19:07,286
Just look at its magnificent form!

203
00:19:07,674 --> 00:19:09,840
Wow, how terrifying...

204
00:19:30,613 --> 00:19:31,681
Lord Sapphire!

205
00:19:31,820 --> 00:19:33,560
Sapphire? What on earth is going on?

206
00:19:33,974 --> 00:19:37,119
Shorty and I caught the hit-and-run driver!

207
00:19:40,929 --> 00:19:42,660
Father, what's gotten into you?!

208
00:19:43,004 --> 00:19:46,500
Having such an evil man build a terrifying new weapon like this!

209
00:19:47,844 --> 00:19:51,566
What are you saying, Lord Sapphire?! This man is a genius!

210
00:19:52,044 --> 00:19:55,449
After all, he built this incredible new weapon!

211
00:19:55,473 --> 00:19:57,860
With this, no country can defeat us!

212
00:19:57,920 --> 00:19:58,536
Shut up!

213
00:19:58,940 --> 00:20:01,293
How can someone who makes killing machines be a genius?!

214
00:20:01,638 --> 00:20:05,083
Oh, Your Majesty, pay no mind to a child's opinion.

215
00:20:05,107 --> 00:20:10,673
Now, quickly set this genius free and pay him as promised.

216
00:20:11,879 --> 00:20:15,800
If there isn't enough in the treasury, collect taxes to cover it.

217
00:20:16,489 --> 00:20:18,496
You bastards! We won't forgive you

218
00:20:18,521 --> 00:20:22,000
if you squeeze taxes out of us poor folks just to buy a monster like this!

219
00:20:22,419 --> 00:20:25,256
Yes, but national defense is necessary.

220
00:20:25,281 --> 00:20:30,700
We could be attacked at any time. We need superior weapons, or else...

221
00:20:31,040 --> 00:20:33,746
Having this won't make Silverland any stronger!

222
00:20:34,374 --> 00:20:39,133
Other countries are bound to make even more powerful weapons, Father!

223
00:20:40,919 --> 00:20:45,096
Your Majesty! This is no time to listen to a child, Your Majesty!

224
00:20:45,121 --> 00:20:45,893
Father!

225
00:20:47,334 --> 00:20:48,673
Open up!

226
00:20:52,499 --> 00:20:56,022
I've had enough! Even if you ask now, I won't sell!

227
00:20:56,047 --> 00:20:57,946
 I'll go sell it to another country!

228
00:20:58,204 --> 00:21:00,980
Wait! Silverland is buying it!

229
00:21:01,399 --> 00:21:03,266
Who cares! So long!

230
00:21:06,060 --> 00:21:07,180
Wait! Please!

231
00:21:07,181 --> 00:21:08,920
Wait!

232
00:21:11,034 --> 00:21:12,280
I won't let you get away!

233
00:21:15,039 --> 00:21:17,586
You fool! Untie me! Untie me!

234
00:21:17,719 --> 00:21:20,386
No! I'm never untying you!

235
00:21:24,514 --> 00:21:27,013
Please! Untie the rope!

236
00:21:29,504 --> 00:21:31,400
Please! Untie the rope!

237
00:21:33,159 --> 00:21:36,980
No! We can't let another country get that flying battleship!

238
00:21:39,989 --> 00:21:41,799
Take this!

239
00:21:57,379 --> 00:21:59,253
Damn it, you actually hung me up!

240
00:22:06,469 --> 00:22:08,666
What?! Fire... H-Hey, someone put it out!

241
00:22:08,779 --> 00:22:11,460
If it catches fire, it's all over!!!

242
00:22:32,759 --> 00:22:34,940
Oh, how terrifying...

243
00:22:40,369 --> 00:22:41,880
Poor thing...

244
00:22:43,859 --> 00:22:48,333
Lord Grandpa, that hit-and-run bastard died. Go easy on him now.

245
00:22:48,358 --> 00:22:50,766
Hmph, what a waste. What a fool.

246
00:22:51,399 --> 00:22:52,873
You're the fool!

247
00:22:53,069 --> 00:22:54,203
Sapphire, I was wrong.

248
00:22:54,228 --> 00:22:57,440
Having such a terrifying new weapon won't make us strong.

249
00:22:57,664 --> 00:23:00,460
Other nations will surely create something even more terrifying.

250
00:23:00,569 --> 00:23:06,400
Father, even without new weapons, I will protect Silverland. I promise.

251
00:23:06,825 --> 00:23:07,825
That's right!

252
00:23:08,779 --> 00:23:10,780
Hearing you say that makes me ashamed of myself.

253
00:23:11,129 --> 00:23:14,809
I'm going to work harder to build a better kingdom for everyone to live in.

254
00:23:14,833 --> 00:23:16,760
Will you help me, Sapphire?

255
00:23:17,809 --> 00:23:18,980
Yes, with pleasure!

256
00:23:19,247 --> 00:23:19,855
Splendid!

257
00:23:20,719 --> 00:23:22,853
Sapphire! I'll help too!

258
00:23:24,799 --> 00:23:27,293
Yeah! We'll all work together!

259
00:23:29,284 --> 00:23:31,284

